course: dictionary
lesson: 1911
title: Combat: fighting and fighting against
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Combat can be a noun, meaning a fight, or a verb, meaning to try hard to stop something.
explain: «Battle fatigue» is an old name for the mental injury soldiers get from combat. The clues are soldiers and battles, so combat means fighting in a war.
explain: Look at the job the word does in the sentence. «Scientists work to combat climate change.» The scientists are not fighting people. They are trying hard to stop or reduce a problem, so combat is a verb here.
fact: «Combat» means fighting, especially between soldiers in war.
fact: «Combat» is often a noun in phrases like «in combat» and «hand-to-hand combat».
fact: «To combat» something means to try hard to stop or reduce it, as in «combat litter» or «combat germs».
fact: «Combat boots» are boots made for fighting in.
fact: A good check is to swap in another word: if «fight» fits in the war sense, combat is the noun; if «stop» or «reduce» fits, combat is the verb.
exercise: «Battle fatigue» is an old name for the mental injury soldiers get from combat. In this sentence, what is combat? | *Fighting in a war | Cooking a meal | A type of cloth | Running a race
exercise: «Scientists work to combat climate change.» What does combat mean here? | Measure carefully | *Try hard to stop or reduce | Forget about | Cheer for
exercise: Which phrase is about fighting in battles? | *Hand-to-hand combat | Combat litter | Combat the spread of disease | Combat germs
test: Which word in «Doctors combat disease with medicine» means to try hard to stop? | disease | medicine | *combat | Doctors
test: «The soldiers were trained for combat.» What does combat mean here? | Cleaning rooms | Reading books | *Fighting in a battle | Sleeping late
exam: Which sentence uses combat as a verb? | *We must combat litter in our park. | Hand-to-hand combat is a fight at close range. | The soldiers stayed in combat for weeks. | Combat boots are strong and warm.
